  <data name="GlossaryTip_Request" xml:space="preserve"><value>The attached transcript (transcript.txt) of "{0}" was made by speech recognition.{1}
Some technical terms, names, case names or product names were written as other words that sound the same or similar.
Please write a glossary for this subject that I can also use for future recordings, in this format (plain text, one entry per line, no numbering or explanations):
- Each misrecognition in the transcript as "wrong -&gt; right". Copy "wrong" exactly as it appears in the transcript (at least 2 characters), e.g. cube cuddle -&gt; kubectl.
- Do not use an ordinary word that is correct elsewhere in the text as "wrong": it is replaced everywhere.
- Leave out corrections you are not sure about.
- Then the important technical terms, names and proper nouns of this field, most important first, at most about 200 lines.
- Lines starting with # are comments.</value></data>
